sis"],"metadata":{"id":"9fhQl0qiD0ru"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["1. Which car has the highest horsepower?\n","\n","Ans: The car with the highest horsepower has better engine power.\n","\n","2. Which car has the highest peak RPM?\n","\n","Ans: The car with the maximum peak RPM has the highest engine speed.\n","\n","3. Which car has the largest engine size?\n","\n","Ans: The car with the largest engine size has a bigger engine.\n","\n","4. How does horsepower affect car performance?\n","\n","Ans: Higher horsepower generally provides more engine power.\n","\n","5. Which car has the highest compression ratio?\n","\n","Ans: The car with the maximum compression ratio has the highest value."],"metadata":{"id":"wXc36rPED6A8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# 8. overall data analysis"],"metadata":{"id":"Ez0Ml5n3EAVw"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["1. What is the total number of rows?\n","\n","Ans: It can be found using the shape function.\n","\n","2. How many columns are present in the dataset?\n","\n","Ans: It can be found using the shape function.\n","\n","3. Are there any missing values?\n","\n","Ans: Missing values can be identified using isnull().\n","\n","4. Are there any duplicate records?\n","\n","Ans: Duplicate records can be identified using duplicated().\n","\n","5. Which numerical columns are highly correlated?\n","\n","Ans: They can be identified using the correlation method"],"metadata":{"id":"LvAu8JKiEFQr"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# automobile dataset report"],"metadata":{"id":"BzOmXFREEK1W"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# 1. INTRODUCTION\n","\n","Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) is the process of analysing a dataset to understand its structure, identify missing values,\n","find patterns and discover useful information.In this project, the Automobile dataset is used to analyse different types of\n","cars based on price, engine size, horsepower, fuel type, mileage and body style.\n","\n","# 2. OBJECTIVES\n","\n","- To understand the Automobile dataset.\n","- To identify missing and duplicate values.\n","- To clean and process the data.\n","- To analyse car prices and brands.\n","- To study engine performance and fuel types.\n","- To analyse mileage and body styles.\n","- To create graphs and visualizations.\n","\n","# 3. DATASET DESCRIPTION\n","\n","The Automobile dataset contains information about different cars and their features.\n","\n","Important columns include:\n","\n","- Make\n","- Fuel Type\n","- Body Style\n","- Drive Wheels\n","- Engine Size\n","- Horsepower\n","- Curb Weight\n","- City MPG\n","- Highway MPG\n","- Price\n","\n","# 4. TOOLS AND TECHNOLOGIES USED\n","\n","- Python\n","- Jupyter Notebook\n","- Pandas\n","- NumPy\n","- Matplotlib\n","- Seaborn\n","\n","# 5. DATA LOADING\n","\n","The dataset is loaded into Jupyter Notebook using Pandas. The first few rows are displayed to understand the data.\n","\n","# 6. DATA CLEANING\n","\n","The dataset is checked for missing values and duplicate records. Missing values are handled, and incorrect\n","data types are converted into suitable formats.\n","\n","# 7. DATA ANALYSIS\n","\n","The following analyses are performed:\n","\n","Car Analysis: Analysed car brands, total cars and body styles.\n","Price Analysis: Identified the highest price, lowest price and average price.\n","Engine Analysis: Analysed engine size, horsepower, engine type and curb weight.\n","Fuel Analysis: Compared petrol and diesel cars.\n","Mileage Analysis: Analysed city mileage and highway mileage.\n","Body Style Analysis: Compared sedan, hatchback and other car body styles.\n","Performance Analysis: Studied horsepower, peak RPM and compression ratio.\n","\n","# 8. DATA VISUALIZATION\n","\n","Matplotlib and Seaborn are used to create graphs and charts.\n","\n","The visualizations help to understand:\n","\n","- Car brand distribution.\n","- Price comparison.\n","- Engine performance.\n","- Fuel type distribution.\n","- Mileage comparison.\n","- Correlation between numerical columns.\n","\n","# 9. KEY FINDINGS\n","\n","The analysis helps to identify popular car brands, price differences, engine performance, fuel types and mileage patterns.\n","\n","The graphs provide a clear understanding of the relationships between different automobile features.\n","\n","# 10. CONCLUSION\n","\n","This project demonstrates how Exploratory Data Analysis can be performed using Python. The Automobile dataset is cleaned,\n","analysed and visualized using Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib and Seaborn.Through this project, we can understand automobile data\n","and identify useful patterns and relationships between different car features.\n","\n","# 11. RESULT\n","\n","Thus, Exploratory Data Analysis of the Automobile dataset was successfully performed using Python and its data analysis libraries."],"metadata":{"id":"iVUct7aSEO2h"}}]}